\newlabel{tab:hodge}{{2}{7}{Hodge content of real RNA-velocity fields: share of $\|f\|^2$ carried by the gradient part, its permutation null, and the part that carries the ground-truth progress. Gastrulation: $n=30{,}000$ cells, E6.5--E8.5 \citep {pijuansala2019single}. RPE1: $n=2{,}793$ cells with FUCCI phase \citep {battich2020sequencing}, velocity from dynamo \citep {qiu2022mapping}}{table.caption.4}{}}
\newlabel{tab:hodge@cref}{{[table][2][]2}{[1][7][]7}}
\newlabel{tab:dsrs}{{3}{7}{Balanced (Sk) versus row-stochastic (RS) Randers affinities built from the same velocity: squared cost, per-row perplexity $\sqrt n$, dense. ``cos'' is the mean cosine between each cell's shift in outgoing displacement, relative to the symmetric affinity, and the gradient or non-gradient Hodge part of the velocity. ``progress'' is the ground-truth progress after $10$ steps of the walk, minus that of the symmetric walk: pseudotime units for pancreas, fractions of a cycle for RPE1. The linear cost gives the same picture}{table.caption.5}{}}
